.TH QIBOCAL 1 "October 2, 2026" "qibocal-report" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qibocal \- serve calibration reports and dispatch interactive notebooks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qibocal
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-\-help ]
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
qibocal-report provides the qibocal command for report servers, local
configuration management, and notebook sessions. Use
.B qibocal COMMAND \-\-help
for the available command options.
.SH NOTEBOOK
.B qibocal notebook
.RI [ CONNECTION ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.PP
Start JupyterLab (default) or Marimo and open its authenticated URL in the
local browser. Keep the command running for the lifetime of the session.
Ctrl+C stops the notebook, releases its SLURM allocation,
and closes the tunnels.
.PP
The connection layers compose:
local machine, optional SSH access node, optional SLURM computing node.
Omitting SSH submits from the local machine. Omitting SLURM runs on the access
node. Omitting both starts a local notebook.
.SS Options
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh " TEXT"
SSH options followed by a host or user@host destination.
Quote the entire value when including options, for example
.BR "\-\-ssh '\-p 2222 \-i ~/.ssh/lab user@login'" .
Host aliases, agent authentication, and jump hosts from SSH configuration work.
The destination must be the last argument; do not include a remote command.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-queue " " \fIPARTITION\fR
SLURM partition passed to srun on the access node.
.TP
.BI \-\-slurm " TEXT"
Additional srun options as a quoted argument string, for example
.BR "\-\-slurm '\-\-time=02:00:00 \-\-account=lab \-\-gres=gpu:1'" .
Specifying this option alone also enables SLURM dispatch.
Resource allocation must select one task on one computing node.
Only common scheduling/resource options are accepted; command, IO,
and working-directory overrides are rejected. Use separated short options
(for example, \-c 2 rather than \-c2).
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-workdir " " \fIDIRECTORY\fR
Change directory on the access node before starting the session or submitting
to SLURM. With SLURM, this directory must also be accessible on the computing
node. Relative kernel paths are resolved in the notebook working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-marimo
Run Marimo instead of JupyterLab.
.TP
.B \-\-jupyter
Use JupyterLab, including when overriding a named Marimo connection.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-interactive
Print the authenticated URL without opening a browser. The command still
stays attached to supervise the notebook and tunnels.
.TP
.B \-\-interactive
Open the browser, including when overriding a named non-interactive connection.
.TP
.BI \-\-venv " NAME_OR_PATH"
Kernel environment on the computing node; default:
.BR qibocal .
Names resolve under
.BR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/qibocal/envs/
(fallback:
.BR ~/.cache/qibocal/envs/ ).
Absolute paths and explicit relative paths (./env or ../env) are used directly.
Existing environments are never overwritten or installed into.
Missing kernel environments are created empty, without pip or packages.
Install Qibocal and your other calibration dependencies into this environment
separately before using them in a notebook.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Maximum startup time, including environment preparation, queue wait, and
tunnel setup. Default: 300. Increase this for long SLURM queue waits.
.SS Requirements and environments
Local execution requires Python 3.10+ with venv support. SSH execution requires
OpenSSH locally and python3 (3.10+) with venv support on the access
and computing nodes. SLURM execution requires srun on the access node
and non-interactive
SSH access from the access node to the allocated computing node, with known
host keys already configured. Notebook servers bind only to loopback.
SLURM sessions tunnel computing-node loopback to access-node loopback; SSH
sessions additionally tunnel access-node loopback to the local machine.
Every session uses a generated authentication token.
.PP
Server dependencies are installed on first use into a separate managed
environment, not the kernel environment. This requires pip and package-index
access on the computing node. Existing server environments are reused as-is.
If first-time installation fails, repair that server environment explicitly
using the command reported by the launcher; it is never implicitly overwritten.
Jupyter exposes the selected environment as the default kernel named
.BR Qibocal .
Its kernel uses that environment's Python and packages, with server-provided
ipykernel dependencies as a fallback. Marimo similarly runs with the selected
environment's Python and uses the separate server's packages as a fallback.
This keeps an existing calibration environment unchanged; server dependencies
may still appear in the notebook's import path.
.SS Named connections
Create a JSON object whose keys are connection names and values are options:
.PP
.nf
{
  "mychip": {
    "ssh": "myuser@login",
    "queue": "mychip",
    "workdir": "/shared/calibration",
    "venv": "qibocal",
    "slurm": "--time=02:00:00",
    "marimo": false,
    "no_interactive": false,
    "timeout": 900
  }
}
.fi
.PP
Save it to
.BR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/qibocal-report/notebooks.json ,
with
.BR ~/.config/qibocal-report/notebooks.json
as the fallback. QIBOCAL_REPORT_CONFIG_DIR overrides its containing directory.
Invoke
.BR "qibocal notebook mychip" .
Explicit command-line options override the connection's values.
Unknown options, invalid types, missing names, and malformed files are errors.
The command does not create or modify the connection file.
.SS Examples
.nf
qibocal notebook
qibocal notebook --venv ./calibration-env --marimo
qibocal notebook --ssh myuser@login --workdir /shared/runs
qibocal notebook --queue mychip --no-interactive
qibocal notebook --ssh myuser@login -q mychip --timeout 900
qibocal notebook mychip --jupyter -n
.fi
.SH REPORT COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "qibocal report server" " [DIRECTORY]"
Serve reports and the embedded web app. Directory defaults to the current
directory. Options: \-\-host (localhost), \-\-port (8000), \-\-auth/\-\-no-auth.
.TP
.B qibocal report client
Serve the standalone report client. Options: \-\-host (127.0.0.1),
\-\-port (8000), \-\-reload.
.TP
.BR "qibocal report dev" " [DIRECTORY]"
Run backend and Vite development servers. Options: \-\-host (localhost),
\-\-port (8000), \-\-frontend-port (5173), \-\-reload/\-\-no-reload,
\-\-auth/\-\-no-auth. Requires the frontend sources and Node.js.
.TP
.BR "qibocal report export" " [OUTPUT_DIR]"
Export the static report client (default: ./dist).
Options: \-\-build/\-\-no-build and \-\-base-path.
.TP
.B qibocal report admin list
List administrators. Options: \-\-all (include all users), \-\-json.
.TP
.BR "qibocal report admin invite" " [USERNAME]"
Generate an administrator invitation. Options: \-u/\-\-username,
\-\-server-url, \-\-host, \-\-port, \-e/\-\-expires-in-hours,
\-\-interactive/\-\-no-interactive, \-\-json.
.BR "qibocal report invite"
is an equivalent shortcut.
.SH CONFIG COMMANDS
.TP
.B qibocal config path
Print the absolute report configuration directory without creating it.
.TP
.B qibocal config clean
Ask before removing servers.json and authentication data.
\-f/\-\-force skips confirmation. Does not remove notebooks.json, notebook
environments, reports, unrelated files, or directories.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Configuration root for notebook connections.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Cache root for computing-node kernel and notebook server environments.
Each node uses its own value; the local value is not forwarded over SSH.
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Location for temporary notebook kernel specifications on the computing node.
When unset or empty, use the system temporary directory.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_REPORT_CONFIG_DIR
Override the local report and notebook connection configuration directory.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_AUTH_FILE
Override the report authentication database.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_REPORT_DIR
Report directory used by the report server.
.TP
.B QIBOCAL_FRONTEND_URL
Frontend development-server URL.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on normal completion or an orderly notebook Ctrl+C shutdown.
Nonzero on invalid configuration, startup failure, timeout, or session failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR srun (1),
.BR python3 (1)
